// EXPECT_RUNTIME_PANIC m280_e3b_panic_names_caller.nv:19 (throw site)
// Plan 280 E3-b (D468): a `throw` inside a function that declares a
// `CallerLoc` parameter stamps the CALLER as the throw site. The marker pins
// line 19, the call; before E3-b this named line 15, the `throw` itself.
//
// This half needed its own runtime door, and the reason is worth knowing
// before touching it: the contract and assert doors COPY the file name into
// their message immediately, so a stack buffer is safe there. The throw doors
// STORE the pointer and read it later, when the panic renders -- so the string
// must be owned. `nova_throw_site_set_dominant_s` interns it in a small static
// pool whose size is derived from the 16-entry trace ring it feeds, not picked.
module standalone.m280_e3b_panic_names_caller

fn boom(msg str, loc CallerLoc = caller_loc()) Fail -> () {
    throw msg
}

fn main() Io -> () {
    boom("exploded")
    println("UNREACHABLE")
}
